WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.945
Bagheera and Kaa finally reached the edge of Monkey City.

2
00:00:06.946 --> 00:00:11.903
They could see Mowgli in a circle with monkeys surrounding him.

3
00:00:11.904 --> 00:00:15.883
The two friends slipped into a ditch.

4
00:00:15.884 --> 00:00:19.609
"I wish Baloo was here," Bagheera whispered.

5
00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:22.425
"But we will do what we can."

6
00:00:22.426 --> 00:00:25.092
He looked up at the sky.

7
00:00:25.093 --> 00:00:29.336
"When that cloud covers the moon, I'll go to the terrace."

8
00:00:29.337 --> 00:00:32.107
"Good luck," Kaa whispered.

9
00:00:32.122 --> 00:00:38.939
"I will go over the west wall." Then he glided away.

10
00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:42.944
*** The monkeys were still giving boastful

11
00:00:42.945 --> 00:00:47.472
speeches. Mowgli saw it was getting

12
00:00:47.473 --> 00:00:53.373
dark. Suddenly he heard something—Bagheera's light feet on the marble

13
00:00:53.374 --> 00:00:59.975
terrace. "It worked!" he thought with relief. "My plan

14
00:00:59.976 --> 00:01:05.287
worked!" With a furious roar, the panther rushed

15
00:01:05.288 --> 00:01:09.579
forward. He darted right and left, striking

16
00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:13.539
monkeys. The startled creatures howled with fright and

17
00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:17.032
rage. Finally a monkey managed to kick

18
00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:22.894
Bagheera. "There's only one attacker!" she shouted. "Let's get

19
00:01:22.895 --> 00:01:27.300
him!" A mass of monkeys surrounded

20
00:01:27.301 --> 00:01:31.217
Bagheera. They were biting, scratching, tearing, and

21
00:01:31.218 --> 00:01:35.077
pulling. Meanwhile another group had grabbed

22
00:01:35.078 --> 00:01:39.523
Mowgli. They dragged him up the wall of a

23
00:01:39.524 --> 00:01:44.414
temple. Then they pushed him through a hole in its broken

24
00:01:44.415 --> 00:01:49.559
dome. A boy raised by humans would have gotten hurt in the fall to the temple

25
00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:53.674
floor. But Mowgli fell exactly as Baloo had taught

26
00:01:53.675 --> 00:01:57.266
him. He landed on his

27
00:01:57.267 --> 00:02:00.125
feet. "Stay in there," a monkey

28
00:02:00.126 --> 00:02:04.464
said. "We'll be back after we get rid of your

29
00:02:04.465 --> 00:02:07.914
friend!" Now Mowgli could hear

30
00:02:07.915 --> 00:02:10.796
Kaa. He quickly gave the snake's

31
00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:13.859
call. There were other snakes inside the

32
00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:17.065
ruins. They hissed back at

33
00:02:17.066 --> 00:02:25.786
him. "Stand still, Little Brother. Please don't step on

34
00:02:25.787 --> 00:02:30.692
us!" Mowgli stood as quietly as he could, peering through a

35
00:02:30.693 --> 00:02:34.751
hole. He listened to the furious sound of Bagheera

36
00:02:34.752 --> 00:02:38.391
fighting. "Baloo must be here too," Mowgli thought.

37
00:02:38.392 --> 00:02:41.276
Bagheera would not have come without him.

38
00:02:41.277 --> 00:02:45.848
"But right now Bagheera could use some help from me."

39
00:02:45.849 --> 00:02:51.712
"Go to the water tank, Bagheera," he shouted. "Get to the water!"

40
00:02:51.713 --> 00:02:54.994
Bagheera heard Mowgli's cry.

41
00:02:54.995 --> 00:02:59.658
"Thank goodness!" the panther thought, fighting his way toward the tanks.

42
00:02:59.659 --> 00:03:02.738
"The man cub is safe!"

43
00:03:02.739 --> 00:03:07.570
Suddenly a shout rose. It was Baloo.

44
00:03:07.571 --> 00:03:11.452
"Bagheera! I'm here!"

45
00:03:11.453 --> 00:03:19.965
The old bear panted as he climbed the terrace.

46
00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:24.896
He threw himself onto his rear legs and held out his paws.

47
00:03:24.897 --> 00:03:30.142
Then he began to hit away monkeys. Bat-bat-bat!

48
00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:34.282
Mowgli heard a crash, followed by a splash.

49
00:03:34.283 --> 00:03:37.325
Bagheera had made it to the water tank!

50
00:03:37.326 --> 00:03:40.544
The monkeys would not follow him in there.

51
00:03:40.545 --> 00:03:45.393
The panther gasped for breath, his head just out of the water.

52
00:03:45.394 --> 00:03:51.178
Monkeys stood on the steps, dancing up and down with rage.

53
00:03:51.179 --> 00:03:56.188
They were ready to spring on him when he came out to help Baloo.

54
00:03:56.189 --> 00:03:59.065
"Where's Kaa?" Bagheera thought.

55
00:03:59.066 --> 00:04:07.501
Had the snake left? He lifted his dripping chin and gave the snake's call.

56
00:04:07.502 --> 00:04:12.639
It had taken Kaa a long time to get over the west wall.

57
00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:21.207
He coiled and uncoiled himself, to be sure that every bit of his long body was working.

58
00:04:21.208 --> 00:04:25.295
Meanwhile, Baloo fought some monkeys.

59
00:04:25.296 --> 00:04:32.365
Mang the bat flew back and forth over them all, carrying the news of the battle.

60
00:04:32.366 --> 00:04:39.499
Then Hathi the elephant trumpeted loudly, waking up birds and more monkeys.

61
00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:44.029
Jungle animals began racing toward Monkey City.

62
00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:49.666
All at once Kaa came—ready to deliver a crushing blow.

63
00:04:49.667 --> 00:04:55.153
The python's first strike drove into the heart of the crowd around Baloo.

64
00:04:55.154 --> 00:04:57.849
He didn't need to strike again.

65
00:04:57.850 --> 00:05:03.023
For all at once the monkeys scattered.

66
00:05:03.023 --> 00:05:10.827
"It's Kaa!" they cried. "Run!"

